cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "GDDiff: Spatially Weighted Guided Diffusion for Face De-Identification"
abstract: >-
  Code for "Reconstruct, Don't Retrain: Spatially Weighted Guided Diffusion for Face
  De-Identification". GDDiff is a training-free face de-identification framework that applies
  Gaussian and Laplacian-of-Gaussian spatial weighting to the data-consistency guidance of a
  pretrained diffusion sampler, with a multi-branch sampler producing three outputs of increasing
  recognizability. Includes the evaluation and revision-analysis scripts.
type: software
version: "1.2"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23576493"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ManfredGonzalez/GDDiff"
keywords:
  - face de-identification
  - diffusion models
  - privacy
